    "turn_text": "That actually leads me to the next question I had, and that is, it's related, and that is, you talk about the Biden administration sort of not looking at Israel and the Israel Palestine conflict. Last Congress, you endorsed a concept. The Middle East Forum has endorsed basically the concept that Israel needs to achieve victory over the Palestinians. That doesn't mean anything specific. It means the idea that this idea that Israel will one day end and just go away, that needs to be taken off the table. How do you think that the further addiction of Israel will or perhaps should affect the Israel-Palestine conflict. And do you think that these recognitions of Israel will help it achieve victory over this idea that its existence will one day end?",
