    "turn_text": "So that on that topic, obviously you would have supported a lot more president Trump's approach to the Middle East, much more than Biden's and so now that we president Biden is now the president. A question I have for you is particularly as. the head of the Republican Study Committee, as I mentioned, with the largest Congress in Congress. You're in a position to both support the administration, if you think it's right, and to propose an alternative as the opposition party. And so, is there any area where you think it's especially important to sort of oppose the Biden administration or, and are there any areas where potentially there might be some agreement in ways that can be worked together?",
