  {
    "episode_id": 76370,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/6/76370.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "Yes, I mean, like you, I'm deeply troubled by the signals of the Biden administration about re-entering the Iran nuclear deal appeasing Iran when all the while we know that appeasement abets weakness and shows weakness on our part that allows for Iran to rebuild their nuclear program to continue to fund their proxy groups. who have done harm and cost the lives of thousands of American troops in different places. It's why we took out Soleimani, the biggest terrorist on the world stage under President Trump's leadership. Why in the world would we agree to reenter a deal that we know was a bad, was a failed deal to begin with? That even after Obama entered into the Iran nuclear deal, Iran continued to build their nuclear program. It wasn't a successful deal in any way to begin with and President Trump was right to get us out of it. In fact, he campaigned on it and it was one of many promises that he made on the campaign trail that he kept. The maximum pressure campaign on Donald Trump and Mike Pompeo, Secretary Mike Pompeo's watch was a successful campaign. And we know that the maximum pressure campaign worked because it dried up resources in Iran, it dried up their economy, it dried up their resources to funnel to their proxy groups. And now the Biden administration wants to reverse it. And because they're attempting to reenter the deal and reverse the maximum pressure campaign, the Republican Study Committee, which I chair, wrote the maximum pressure act. We introduced it yesterday. We have nearly 90 co-sponsors. If not over 90 co-sponsors at the moment, I expect many more to sign on to it as it gets more attention. in the days to come. And it was great. Cliff, by the way, to have Secretary Pompeo join us out in the triangle in front of the Capitol yesterday as we unveiled this major piece of legislation because we wanted to send a signal to the Ayatollah and to Joe Biden. If you re-enter the Iran nuclear deal and reverse all of the sanctions on Iran, it's not going to last for long because Republicans are going to win the majority. in the midterms in 2022 we're going to put those sanctions back in place right away once we take back control and force force the hand of the Biden administration there's also another component of this I want to talk about for a moment and that's the proper role of the legislative branch of government the Congress. The Obama administration is circumvented Congress by not passing this as a treaty through the Senate when he signed on to the Iran nuclear deal. It's shameful. And it appears that the Biden administration is going to take the same path forward. And the maximum pressure act that I introduced with almost 90 of my colleagues is Congress reasserting its proper role in this in this equation is something that you can count on a Republican study committee and conservatives like me to continue to do in the future.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
