    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/6/76370.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 21,
    "turn_text": "But on President Biden's watch, again, we're seeing a new president take office and in his earliest days has very little, shows very few signs of actually holding the Chinese Communist Party accountable and reasserting America's role to circumvent the debt trap diplomacy that you describe that China is employing in the Middle East. Why does it matter to us? It matters to us because for China to diplomatically assert themselves in areas where the United States has historically enjoyed strong relationships with countries like Saudi Arabia, the UAE, Israel, Egypt, other countries that those are, by the way, those are four of the five countries that President Trump's ambassador to Israel, David Friedman warned that China was building up in the Middle East more than elsewhere, Israel and Iran. So Saudi Arabia, the UAE, Egypt, Israel and Iran, and a couple of those countries a few of those countries are very important partners, and a couple of them are obviously not. But China's debt trap diplomacy puts them in a position and a situation where they can leverage those investments and these new relationships that they're building. to use that leverage against the United States of America. I mean, that is the Chinese Communist Party's in goal is to dominate the United States of America. They know that if they can entangle themselves in places where the United States has historically enjoyed strong relationships like with Israel, China knows that that's one way, one way to accelerate their dominance over the United States economically and militarily. in the long term. So that's deeply troubling to me. And what's even more troubling is that the Biden administration has so far has turned a complete blind eye to any efforts. that were started under President Trump or because they were started under President Trump, President Biden is no interest in continuing efforts that would hold the Chinese Communist Party accountable and to reassert our leadership in places where it's desperately needed. So that's something that I worked on extensively in my work here on Capitol Hill and on the Armed Services Committee and something that I appreciate the work that you all do and look forward to partnering more with you on in the future.",
