    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "Again, another very important question. I participate as a member of the Afghanistan caucus, the Pakistan caucus, the India caucus. I've taken a significant role in all of these caucuses because I believe that to bring stability to that region, we have to figure out what our strategy is moving forward. I'm often critical of the Biden administration, but these were areas as well were too often during the Trump era and the Trump administration. There was an erratic strategy that often that often changed too quickly to keep up or didn't make sense and creating a way forward to address some of these issues over the last four years as well. So that being said, the The Mike Pompeo led State Department made strong gains on tackling some of these developing strategies to combat some of these terrorist groups and other elements. So far, in the first three months of the Biden administration, I've seen little effort or interest. in the Middle East at all, but especially on addressing some of these threats that are important, not just the United States, but to our allies like Israel. And that's unfortunate too. I mean, again, at the outset of our conversation, Cliff, how is it that President Biden still has not nominated an ambassador to Israel, our most important ally, at least in the Middle East? if not altogether the most important ally that we have around the world, whose interests are most closely aligned with the interests of the United States of America. How is it that he has even nominated an ambassador yet to serve in that important post? It's because there's so little attention or desire to address these issues on behalf of this new administration that should be deeply traveling to all of us. That and the rising threat and violence that we're seeing from ISIS, al-Qaeda, Taliban, other terrorist groups in this region is something that the Biden administration, apparently, they just hope it will go away. It's not going to go away if we don't have the strategy to combat it. And as a member of Congress, my job pushed the administration to do that.",
